            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all five changed paths in full. The change adds ParseReport/Clear for an exemption report and generalizes checkShape in wire.go to take the list member name and item members; the verdict path passes 'verdicts' and verdictMembers, keeping its prior behavior and error wording (pinned by the new test in parse_test.go).",
              "Input handling is unchanged in strictness: UTF-8 check, duplicate-key check, strict object member checks, and jsonstrict.DecodeStrict are applied to the report path the same as to verdicts. No file reads, command execution, secrets, network, or new dependencies are introduced.",
              "Clear() fails closed: an empty checks list, a failed check, or a not-run check is never treated as clear, and check() requires a recognized result plus non-blank command and output. No authorization or data-exposure issue is reachable from this candidate; ParseReport has no callers in the diff that grant anything."
            ]
          }
        }
