            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "wire.go: checkShape is parameterized by list name and members. The verdicts call passes \"verdicts\" and verdictMembers, so the refusal strings for the reply shape keep their wording (\"verdicts is not an array\", \"verdicts[%d]\"). The new test in engine/reviewverdict/parse_test.go pins those messages.",
              "report.go: ParseReport runs the shape check, then the strict decode, then each check in order, with the enumeration checked before the evidence. Every refusal wraps one Err value and returns the empty Report. Clear rejects an empty report and any check that is not pass, so a check that did not run never counts as passing.",
              "report_test.go covers ordering of the checks, the first-broken-rule precedence, unknown members, enum violations, missing evidence, and Clear for failed, not-run and empty reports. It also covers the cross-rejection between Parse and ParseReport, so the new behavior is proved at the unit level.",
              "Unverifiable from the candidate: the \"empty\" wording asserted for an empty or whitespace-only report depends on the unchanged jsonstrict and strictObject helpers, which are not part of the patch. I could not show it fails, so I report no finding."
            ]
          }
